.TH DRAW3D 2
.SH NAME
draw3d: init, context, resize, setzarea, clearz, setz, setzclip, setcolour, settransform, viewport, mode, push, pop, identity, translate, scale, rotatex, rotatey, rotatez, rotate, frustum, ortho, loadmatrix, storematrix, matmul, project, mulpoint, begin, vertex, circle, ellipse, end, line3, plot3, fillpoly3, sprite3, sprite3zb, sprite3yb, sprite3mat, newmatrix, vdot, vcross, vnorm \- immediate-mode 3-D drawing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "draw.m";
include "math/polyfill.m";
include "math/draw3d.m";
draw3d := load Draw3d Draw3d->PATH;
Vector, Matrix: import draw3d;

ZSCALE: con real (1<<20);
MODEL, PROJ: con iota;
POLY, FILLPOLY, CIRCLE, FILLCIRCLE, ELLIPSE, FILLELLIPSE: con iota;

Vector: adt { x, y, z: real; };
Matrix: type array of array of real;

Context: adt {
	dst:       ref Draw->Image;
	zstate:    ref Polyfill->Zstate;
	zenable:   int;
	clipbehind:int;
	colour:    ref Draw->Image;
	transform: ref fn(v: Vector): Vector;
	mx, cx, my, cy: real;
};

init:        fn();
context:     fn(dst: ref Draw->Image): ref Context;
resize:      fn(c: ref Context, dst: ref Draw->Image);
setzarea:    fn(c: ref Context, r: Draw->Rect);
clearz:      fn(c: ref Context);
setz:        fn(c: ref Context, on: int);
setzclip:    fn(c: ref Context, on: int);
setcolour:   fn(c: ref Context, col: ref Draw->Image);
settransform:fn(c: ref Context, t: ref fn(v: Vector): Vector);
viewport:    fn(c: ref Context, x1, y1, x2, y2: int);

mode:        fn(which: int);
push, pop, identity: fn();
translate:   fn(x, y, z: real);
scale:       fn(x, y, z: real);
rotatex, rotatey, rotatez: fn(deg: real);
rotate:      fn(deg, l, m, n: real);
frustum:     fn(l, n, f: real);
ortho:       fn(l, n, f: real);
loadmatrix:  fn(m: Matrix);
storematrix: fn(m: Matrix);
matmul:      fn();

project:     fn(c: ref Context, v: Vector): (Draw->Point, real, int);
mulpoint:    fn(m: Matrix, v: Vector): Vector;

begin:       fn(c: ref Context, kind, nvert: int);
vertex:      fn(c: ref Context, x, y, z: real): (real, real);
circle:      fn(c: ref Context, x, y, z, r: real);
ellipse:     fn(c: ref Context, x, y, z: real, axes: Vector);
end:         fn(c: ref Context);

line3:       fn(c: ref Context, a, b: Vector, thick: int);
plot3:       fn(c: ref Context, v: Vector);
fillpoly3:   fn(c: ref Context, verts: array of Vector, normal: Vector, lit: real);

sprite3:     fn(c: ref Context, p: Vector, img, mask: ref Draw->Image, scale: real);
sprite3zb:   fn(c: ref Context, p: Vector, img, mask: ref Draw->Image, scale, degz: real);
sprite3yb:   fn(c: ref Context, p: Vector, img, mask: ref Draw->Image, scale: real);
sprite3mat:  fn(c: ref Context, p: Vector, m: Matrix, img, mask: ref Draw->Image, scale: real);

newmatrix:   fn(): Matrix;
vdot:        fn(a, b: Vector): real;
vcross:      fn(a, b: Vector): Vector;
vnorm:       fn(v: Vector): Vector;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Draw3d
.RB ( /dis/math/draw3d.dis )
provides a small immediate-mode 3-D API for Inferno applications.
It is used by
.IR draw3ddemo (1)
and by the programs in
.IR temple (1).
The module keeps a dual matrix stack (model and projection), projects
.B Vector
values into a destination
.IR Draw
.BR Image ,
and can depth-test filled surfaces through
.IR polyfill (2).
.PP
The interface is defined once in
.B math/draw3d.m .
An alternate implementation,
.BR /dis/math/draw3ddev.dis ,
implements the same
.B Draw3d
module type but encodes
.BR fillpoly3 ,
.BR line3 ,
.BR plot3 ,
sprites, and related state through optional
.IR draw (3)
protocol letters
.RB ( 3 / M / w / u / z / g / G / h / j / k / q )
so a capable
.B /dev/draw
server can rasterise or Metal-accelerate the primitives.
Clients choose the provider by which
.B .dis
they
.BR load ;
.B Draw3d->PATH
remains the software module.
.PP
.B Init
must be called once after the module is loaded.
.B Context
binds drawing to a destination image and returns a
.B Context
adt.
.B Resize
retargets an existing context after the window image changes.
.B Viewport
sets the NDC-to-screen mapping so that normalised device coordinates map into
the pixel rectangle
.BI (x1 , y1 )-( x2 , y2) .
.B Setcolour
selects the pen
.B Image
used by vector primitives.
.B Settransform
installs an optional foreshortening callback;
.B nil
means identity.
When
.B settransform
is set,
.B draw3ddev
sends an identity model matrix and applies model+transform in Limbo before
.B g / G / k / h / j
so Castle-style foreshortening stays correct.
.PP
.BR Setzarea ,
.BR clearz ,
and
.B setz
allocate, clear, and enable a software z-buffer covering rectangle
.IR r .
Plane depths written by
.B fillpoly3
use the fixed-point scale
.BR ZSCALE ,
matching
.IR polyfill (2)
and
.BR wm/polyhedra .
With
.BR draw3ddev ,
.B clearz
also clears the server z-buffer
.RB ( z )
and Metal depth;
soft fallback inside the emu uses the same plane coefficients when the GPU
cannot draw (obscured or off-screen destinations).
.B Setzclip
enables rejection of geometry with eye-space
.B z ≥ 0
(appropriate for a perspective frustum); leave it clear for orthographic scenes.
.SS Matrix stack
.B Mode
selects the active stack:
.B MODEL
or
.BR PROJ .
.BR Push ,
.BR pop ,
and
.B identity
have the usual meanings.
.BR Translate ,
.BR scale ,
.BR rotatex ,
.BR rotatey ,
.BR rotatez ,
and
.B rotate
(angle in degrees about unit axis
.IR (l,m,n) )
post-multiply the current matrix.
.B Frustum
and
.B ortho
are symmetric helpers taking half-width
.IR l ,
near
.IR n ,
and far
.IR f .
.B Loadmatrix
and
.B storematrix
transfer a 4×4
.BR Matrix ;
.B matmul
replaces the current matrix with the product of the projection and model
matrices (the MVP used by subsequent drawing).
.SS Projection and primitives
.B Project
transforms a world-space
.B Vector
and returns a screen
.BR Point ,
the eye-space
.IR z ,
and a non-zero ok flag when the point is not clipped.
.B Mulpoint
applies an explicit matrix.
.PP
.BR Line3 ,
.BR plot3 ,
and
.B fillpoly3
draw lines, points, and filled polygons in world space.
.B Fillpoly3
takes a face
.I normal
(same space as the vertices) and a lighting factor
.IR lit ;
when z-buffering is enabled it computes plane coefficients for
.IR polyfill (2).
On the protocol path
.RB ( k ),
.I lit
scales solid colours in the server/Metal; the pure software module expects
the caller to tint
.B c.colour
(TempleOS style).
.PP
Immediate mode follows a GL-ish pattern:
.B begin
selects a primitive kind
.RB ( POLY ,
.BR FILLPOLY ,
.BR CIRCLE ,
.BR FILLCIRCLE ,
.BR ELLIPSE ,
.BR FILLELLIPSE )
and an expected vertex count;
.B vertex
emits a point (returning the projected pair for callers that need it);
.B circle
and
.B ellipse
are convenience emitters;
.B end
flushes the primitive.
With
.BR draw3ddev ,
.B POLY / FILLPOLY
use
.B line3 / fillpoly3
(Metal
.B G / k );
.B CIRCLE / ELLIPSE
use letter
.B q
(Metal tessellation);
sprites use letter
.B j
(Metal textured quads with depth).
.SS Sprites
The Sprite3 family draws an image (with optional mask) as a camera-facing billboard.
.I Scale
is a world-space half-width; 0 uses the image width in pixels.
.B sprite3
places an upright billboard;
.B sprite3yb
applies a vertical squash (yaw billboard stand-in);
.B sprite3zb
rotates about Z (Metal screen-space rotation on the protocol path);
.B sprite3mat
uses an explicit matrix.
.B draw3ddev
encodes sprites as letter
.BR j .
.PP
.BR Newmatrix ,
.BR vdot ,
.BR vcross ,
and
.B vnorm
are small vector/matrix helpers.
.SH EXAMPLE
Typical per-frame setup inside a
.IR wmclient (2)
redraw:
.EX
	draw3d->resize(c, img);
	draw3d->mode(Draw3d->PROJ);
	draw3d->identity();
	draw3d->frustum(1.0, 1.0, 100.0);
	draw3d->mode(Draw3d->MODEL);
	draw3d->identity();
	draw3d->translate(0.0, 0.0, -8.0);
	draw3d->rotatey(ang);
	draw3d->setcolour(c, yellow);
	draw3d->line3(c, Vector(-1.0,0.0,0.0), Vector(1.0,0.0,0.0), 1);
.EE
